&lt;p&gt;Job Title: Staff Software Engineer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: SF Bay Area&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Canopy&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Canopy, we build technology that helps make healthcare environments safer for the people delivering care. Our connected safety platform powers real-time communication, response coordination, and location intelligence across hospitals and complex care environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate in high-trust, high-reliability environments where software quality, operational resilience, and customer experience matter deeply. Our engineering organization is scaling alongside our growth, and we are looking for a Staff Software Engineer who can help shape both our technical direction and the way we build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not simply a feature delivery role. This is a systems-thinking role for an experienced engineer who can drive architecture, influence engineering standards, and help scale a platform, organization, and culture simultaneously.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Canopy is seeking a Staff Software Engineer to develop our next-generation sensing data pipeline — building the “physical full stack” from firmware and edge algorithms to the backend and frontend services that power them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will bridge physical hardware and cloud systems, applying physics-based modeling to solve complex sensing challenges at scale that are not possible with traditional products. This is a unique role within Canopy to translate hardware schematics and firmware design into products that work in harsh environments and result in life-saving outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care deeply about building highly automated development environments that accelerate our prototyping and verification cycles, ensuring our mission-critical systems are built faster, safer, and with greater precision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How to you will make 10X impact:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the development of next-generation hardware that will be in the hands of millions of healthcare professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement robust firmware across Canopy devices; build and maintain a powerful HIL automation platform to accelerate development and enforce system safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply signal processing and machine learning for on-device algorithms, cloud pipelines, and field-ops tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across hardware product and software teams to launch production-grade sensing devices at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply systems-level design intuition to compute layers power management and communication protocols&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer industrial-grade fault-tolerant designs to ensure reliability during unexpected power events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We’re excited about you because:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy building, and thrive in teams that care a lot about people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep proficiency in Rust, C, C++, Python with practical experience in RTOS (Real-Time Operation System) (e.g., Zephyr, FreeRTOS) and Embedded Linux (e.g., Yocto, Buildroot).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intuitive grasp of digital electronics, board-level bring-up/validation/debugging, BSP (Board Support Package) and peripheral communication (SPI, I2C, UART, and interrupt-driven design).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to troubleshoot complex systems using oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, and diagnostic tools at the hardware/software boundary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building deterministic, timing-sensitive firmware that integrates effectively with cloud-native data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find extraordinarily creative ways to amass training data quickly to develop production-grade algorithms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s, Master&#39;s, or PhD in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;It’d be great if you also had these:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in applied signal processing, machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in healthcare, GIS, safety-critical, or high-availability environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling SaaS platforms through periods of rapid growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with event-driven architectures, real-time systems, or location-aware platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity or interest in contributing to…&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distributed systems, APIs, and service-oriented architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern full-stack application development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DevOps, SRE, or platform engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How We Work&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Canopy, strong engineers do more than write code. We value people who:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Care deeply about the customer and mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act with intention and intellectual curiosity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own outcomes, not just tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Win together through collaboration and trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an engineering culture that prioritizes high standards, thoughtful execution, and continuous improvement — without ego or heroics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Join Canopy&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on technology with real-world impact in healthcare environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence architecture and engineering direction at a critical stage of company growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with high autonomy and meaningful ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with a mission-driven, highly capable team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape how a scaling engineering organization operates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Canopy is an equal opportunity employer committed to building diverse teams and an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re excited about the opportunity to work on groundbreaking projects, collaborate with a talented team, and make a positive impact on the lives of healthcare workers, we&#39;d love to hear from you. Join us in making a difference, from anywhere in the world, and apply now!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this position is $200k - $225k per year, depending on location, experience and qualifications. Canopy is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Account Executive – National Health Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Remote, U.S. | Travel Required&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt; Sales&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Canopy, we&#39;re on a mission to make healthcare safer for the people who dedicate their lives to caring for others. Our connected safety platform helps healthcare organizations protect their teams, respond to incidents, and create environments where caregivers can focus on delivering exceptional care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;ve established a strong foundation with leading healthcare organizations. Now we&#39;re looking for an exceptional &lt;strong&gt;Strategic Account Executive&lt;/strong&gt; to help us win the next generation of transformational customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn&#39;t a traditional territory-based sales role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own a select portfolio of the nation&#39;s largest and most influential healthcare organizations — complex, multi-hospital, multi-region systems with the potential to become some of Canopy&#39;s most significant customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission is to open doors that others can&#39;t, build relationships where none exist, navigate complex organizational dynamics, and turn ambitious opportunities into long-term enterprise partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be a &lt;strong&gt;hunter first and a strategic account owner second.&lt;/strong&gt; You won&#39;t inherit a mature book of business or rely on inbound opportunities. You&#39;ll create the opportunity, win the initial business, and own the commercial relationship as it expands across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person will see a health system with hundreds of facilities, multiple decision-makers, and a complicated procurement process — and see an opportunity worth pursuing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Open doors into the nation&#39;s largest healthcare organizations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a discrete portfolio of named strategic accounts, separate from Canopy&#39;s regional Enterprise AE territories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute account strategies to penetrate large, complex healthcare systems where Canopy has limited or no existing presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify, engage, and build relationships with senior executives, including CEOs, COOs, CFOs, CNOs, security executives, and other influential stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create opportunities through executive networking, industry relationships, targeted prospecting, referrals, and creative business development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a deep understanding of each target organization&#39;s structure, strategic priorities, purchasing processes, and internal decision-making dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Orchestrate and win complex, transformational deals&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead sophisticated, multi-stakeholder sales cycles involving clinical leadership, security, operations, IT, finance, procurement, and executive sponsors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop compelling business cases that connect workforce safety, operational effectiveness, employee experience, and financial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate decentralized decision-making, complex contracting requirements, and lengthy procurement cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align internal teams across Sales, Product, Customer Experience, and executive leadership to build solutions and deal strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate enterprise agreements and commercial structures that support both an initial deployment and substantial future expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personally own the deal strategy, momentum, executive alignment, and commercial close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Turn the initial win into an enterprise-wide opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat the first sale as the beginning of the relationship, not the finish line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a strategic account plan that maps expansion opportunities across facilities, regions, and business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain executive relationships and commercial ownership following the initial sale, partnering closely with Customer Experience on successful adoption and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify new buying centers, additional use cases, and opportunities to expand Canopy&#39;s footprint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build long-term, trusted relationships that position Canopy as a strategic partner rather than a point solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure account growth is deliberate, repeatable, and supported by measurable customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Build the playbook for strategic account selling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with Canopy&#39;s SVP Sales and executive team to develop innovative approaches to winning transformational accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build account intelligence, stakeholder maps, competitive strategies, and multi-year growth plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring customer and market intelligence back to Product, Marketing, and leadership to influence Canopy&#39;s strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create repeatable approaches for enterprise-wide sales and expansion that can scale as our strategic accounts business grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with exceptional discipline in forecasting, pipeline management, and resource allocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You Successful&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who has already demonstrated the ability to win business that others consider too large, complex, or difficult to pursue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re a proven big-game hunter.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve personally opened doors into major enterprise organizations, created opportunities from scratch, and converted them into meaningful revenue. You don&#39;t rely on an inherited pipeline, established relationships alone, or an SDR team to generate your success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You understand how large health systems buy.&lt;/strong&gt; You know how to navigate the complexity of integrated delivery networks, multiple hospitals, corporate versus local decision-making, clinical stakeholders, and sophisticated procurement organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You can operate in the boardroom and the hallway.&lt;/strong&gt; You are as comfortable presenting a strategic business case to a health system CEO as you are walking a hospital floor to understand frontline needs. You know that influencing the executive sponsor and earning credibility with the people using the product are equally important.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You play the long game without losing urgency.&lt;/strong&gt; You can manage extended sales cycles while consistently creating momentum, advancing stakeholder relationships, and finding opportunities for near-term wins.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re a strategic thinker who executes relentlessly.&lt;/strong&gt; You can develop a multi-year account strategy but aren&#39;t afraid to pick up the phone, make the introduction, conduct the discovery call, or drive the next meeting yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You build partnerships, not just transactions.&lt;/strong&gt; While your primary instinct is to hunt, you have the judgment and relationship skills to grow an account over time — without becoming a passive account manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of successful enterprise or strategic sales experience, preferably in healthcare technology, enterprise software, or complex technology solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience selling into large U.S. health systems, integrated delivery networks (IDNs), or similarly complex healthcare organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success personally sourcing, developing, negotiating, and closing large, multi-stakeholder, enterprise-level deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of winning new logos and subsequently expanding those relationships across additional facilities, business units, or regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and credibility with C-suite stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with navigating long sales cycles, complex procurement structures, and enterprise contracting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional account planning, relationship mapping, negotiation, and business case development skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to succeed in a high-growth environment where creativity, resilience, urgency, and personal accountability matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel regularly to target accounts, industry events, and customer sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Especially compelling:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience selling into the largest national health systems or government healthcare organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships with senior decision-makers across major healthcare networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with workforce safety, healthcare operations, security technology, connected devices, or enterprise-wide infrastructure deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing initial deployments that ultimately grew into major multi-site or national agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 90 days:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a clear strategic plan for your portfolio of named accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map executive stakeholders, decision-making structures, and entry points within priority systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish meaningful engagement with decision-makers and influencers at target organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a credible pipeline and actionable pursuit plans for priority opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In your first 6–12 months:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate qualified, executive-sponsored opportunities within the strategic account portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance priority accounts through clearly defined buying and procurement milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure initial strategic wins where sales-cycle timing permits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish expansion strategies for landed accounts that create pathways to materially larger enterprise opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
